WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.979
In this guide, we will create a rule that blocks the word promotion,

2
00:00:03.979 --> 00:00:07.958
and apply it to just one app.

3
00:00:07.958 --> 00:00:11.750
Open Rules from the bottom navigation, then select the Rules tab at the

4
00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:15.542
top of the screen.

5
00:00:15.542 --> 00:00:20.167
Tap Add rule. This opens the rule editor, where you choose what to

6
00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:24.792
block and which app the rule applies to.

7
00:00:24.792 --> 00:00:28.208
For this example, choose Block a word or phrase from the Rule type

8
00:00:28.208 --> 00:00:31.625
menu.

9
00:00:31.625 --> 00:00:36.146
Enter promotion in the Word or phrase field. This is the text the

10
00:00:36.146 --> 00:00:40.667
rule will look for in notifications.

11
00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:47.083
Tap Applies to and select your app, for example Gmail. All apps applies

12
00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:53.500
the rule across apps. Select a specific app to limit its scope.

13
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:58.750
If your app is missing, make sure silenQo has notification access, then let

14
00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:04.000
that app send a notification and check the list again.

15
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.917
Check that Applies to shows Gmail, then tap Add block rule to save.

16
00:01:09.917 --> 00:01:15.833
Keep filtering enabled on Home for the rule to block matching notifications.

17
00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:21.292
Your rule now targets notifications containing promotion from Gmail. You can review it

18
00:01:21.292 --> 00:01:26.750
under Rules, and tap it later to edit.

